Purpose of CosmoLapse
=====================
This thorn calculates and provides

proper time
-----------

starting from tau = code time
 >> d(tau)/dt = abs(alpha^2 - beta^i beta^j g_{ij})^(1/2)

gauge
-----

 ---- Lapse ----

 >> d(alpha)/dt = - alpha^2 fBM (Ka - Kb)

. fBM = fBMa + fBMb alpha^fBMc
with user defined "fBMa", "fBMb", "fBMc"

. Ka = [K, softplus]
user chooses between them with "KaExpression"
with softplus: Ln[1 + Exp[S (K - T)]] / S + T
tuned with used defined S = "KaSteepness" and T = "KaTransition"
 '-> T is updated to be = - max(-T, Ka) if "KaTransitionExp" = 1

. Kb = [0, Kth, - sqrt(24 pi rho (1 + eps))]
user chooses between them with "KbExpression"
with Kth = - 2.0 / (tau (1 + eosw)) 
and eosw = press / (rho (1 + eps)) using terms from HydroBase

 ---- Shift ----

 >> d(beta^i)/dt = betaXi1 B^i
 >> d(B^i)/dt = betaXi2 alpha^betaP d(Xt^i)/dt - betaEta beta^i
with user defined "betaXi1", "betaXi2", "betaP", "betaEta"

 ---- Advection ----

 >> d()/dt = ... + \beta^k \partial_k ()
The user can include the Lie derivative advection terms by setting 
 "alphaFullLieDeriv" and "betaFullLieDeriv". 
And can choose if these are upwinded with "upwind".

