How to implement this thorn into Einstein Toolkit:
==================================================
===== 1) Have a working version of Einstein Toolkit
# Follow the instructions here
# https://github.com/nds-org/jupyter-et/blob/master/tutorial-server/notebooks/CactusTutorial.ipynb
# Don't forget to try to run HelloWorld

#If you're doing this on an HPC
>> cd pathtocactus
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim setup-silent --machine=HPCname
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim build --machine=HPCname --thornlist=thornlists/einsteintoolkit.th

#The paths of the HPC config files are:
# pathtocactus/simfactory/mdb/machines/HPCname.ini
# pathtocactus/simfactory/mdb/optionlists/HPCname.cfg
# pathtocactus/simfactory/mdb/runscripts/HPCname.run
# pathtocactus/simfactory/mdb/submitscripts/HPCname.sub

===== 2) Include CosmoLapse in Einstein Toolkit
# link
>> cd path_to_Cactus/Cactus/arrangements/EinsteinEvolve/
>> ln -s path_to_thorn/CosmoThorn/CosmoLapse .
# add to Cactus/thornlists/einsteintoolkit.th, in EinsteinEvolve section
EinsteinEvolve/CosmoLapse

===== 3) Compile Einstein Toolkit
# in Cactus directory
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim build -j2 --thornlist=thornlists/einsteintoolkit.th
# Or
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim build --machine=HPCname --thornlist=thornlists/einsteintoolkit.th

===== 4) Run test_CosmoLapse.par to check if it works
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim create-submit test_CosmoLapse --parfile=path/to/CosmoThorn/test_CosmoLapse.par --procs=1 --num-threads=1
# Or
>> ./simfactory/bin/sim create-submit test_CosmoLapse --machine=HPCname --parfile=path/to/CosmoThorn/test_CosmoLapse.par --procs=1 --num-threads=1
eventhough the example uses ICPertFLRW_GRH, this is not a requirement

===== 5) Check output
with
 >> tail -30 ~/simulations/test_CosmoLapse/output-0000/test_CosmoLapse.out
you should get:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
